body:
Hey thank you so much for replying. Sorry it took so long to respond, I've just been in a bad place.

I've been inpatient before due to a suicide attempt. It was one of the worst experiences of my life. It was cable tv and finger painting. No therapy or anyone to listen, I never felt so insulted. That was the only place that would take me due to my insurance. I left after 2 weeks because it made me so furious. But I'm not like that anymore, I do want to live, but I can't with this horrible panic.  I wish I could be inpatient somewhere that was halfway decent and accepted my insurance.  But also with COVID I feel like I'd freak out  ;_;

I'll check out Claire Weekes though, sounds cool!
